p for p,t in page_text.items() if norm(q) in norm(t)]\n    print(k, '->', hits)\n\n# inspect page 51 table region\nt51 = page_text.get(51,'')\nlines51 = t51.split('\\n')\nprint('==== P51 keyword region ====')\nidx=set()\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines51):\n    low=l.lower()\n    if any(x in low for x in ['topic','training data','hallucination','agent behavior','self reflection','safety','agenda']):\n        idx.update(range(max(0,i-1), min(len(lines51), i+4)))\nprint('\\n'.join(lines51[i] for i in sorted(idx))[:3000])\nprint('==== P52 conclusion ====')\nt52 = page_text.get(52,'')\nlines52 = t52.split('\\n')\nidx2=set()\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines52):\n    if any(x in l.lower() for x in ['benefit from','conclusion','table 4','five']):\n        idx2.update(range(max(0,i-2), min(len(lines52), i+3)))\nprint('\\n'.join(lines52[i] for i in sorted(idx2))[:2500])\n```","reasoning_content":"Let me assess the state. The plan shows baseline done, extraction doing, notes todo. But actually notes already exist for all five topics (model-authored notes shown in progress). PDF pages missing: [] — so all 52 pages extracted. The remaining work: merge notes into report.json, verify with pytest.\n\nWait, the previous action excerpt shows I did read individual pages via read_pdf.py per page (1,5,10,13,21,23,37,47) plus earlier a full-range extraction presumably. `pdf_pages_missing: []` means the required full read is satisfied.\n\nAlso \"Not fully delivered yet\" evidence for pages from a batch — but evidence delivery is for the model's benefit; I already have the notes with quotes.\n\nNow the task: write report.json with the five sections. Then run pytest. Requests left: 11. So be efficient: write report.json in maybe 2-3 actions, run pytest, final answer.\n\nBut careful: \"first_write_reading_required\": true — I must have read report.json fully before writing; full_reads_registered includes report.json, so ok.\n\nLet me check current report.json content? Its hash is of \"{}\"? The regis